msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Tool filtering, IP restrictions and usage sharing — most sites never need to change these."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Minimum capability for External Data tools"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "The lowest WordPress capability that can call the Google Analytics, Search Console, DataForSEO, Semrush and SE Ranking tools. They default to administrators only; lower this to let editors or authors use them. Tools a user cannot call are also hidden from the client’s tool list. Ahrefs is unaffected and stays available to any authorized user."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Max title length"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "characters"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "The longest title a tool may set on a post or page. 0 turns the limit off; a longer title makes the tool return an error."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Disabled tools"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Checked tools are disabled for every client and return an error when called, whatever the token allows."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "The full tree, category by category, is under <link>Tools › Core</link>."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Whitelist tools"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Comma-separated glob patterns matched against tool names. A tool is available if its name matches any pattern; * is a wildcard. A pattern without a wildcard matches any tool whose name contains it, so post matches wp_get_post."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Be careful"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "When set, only tools whose names match one of these patterns are available — for every token. This can break existing workflows. Leave empty to allow all tools."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "IP whitelist"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "One IP address or CIDR range per line, e.g. 203.0.113.10 or 192.168.1.0/24. Leave empty to allow all addresses."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Applies to every request on the MCP endpoint, with an API key or an OAuth grant alike. A request from an address that is not listed is refused with 403 and recorded in the audit log. Cloud clients such as claude.ai and ChatGPT connect from the vendor’s servers, not from the user’s machine — for those users either list the vendor’s IP ranges or leave this empty."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Behind a reverse proxy, load balancer or CDN such as Cloudflare, WordPress sees the proxy’s address for every visitor, so this list, the rate limits and the audit log cannot tell visitors apart. Declare the proxy with the <code>EASY_MCP_AI_TRUSTED_PROXIES</code> constant in wp-config.php — see <a>Trusted proxies</a>."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Not recorded at all"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Anything you or your team change yourselves — edits in WordPress admin, WP-CLI, other plugins. This log covers AI assistant activity only."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Changes sent to an outside service, such as a push-notification or email-marketing provider. We record that it happened and which service was contacted, but not what changed over there."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Files written to disk — backups, generated images, code-snippet files."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Work that finishes after the assistant's request ends, such as queued or scheduled jobs. The same action can be fully recorded on a small site and missed on a busy one, because size is what pushes a plugin into queuing."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "A few plugins switch off WordPress's change notifications before saving. Unless \"Capture raw database writes\" is turned on, we can only note that this happened."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Recorded, but not in full"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "One database command that updates thousands of rows appears as a single entry showing one example row. The number of rows affected is not shown."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "The body text of posts and pages is not stored here — use the linked revision to see it. Some content types, including WooCommerce products, keep no revisions, and revisions can also be switched off site-wide. Where that is the case the entry says so plainly, and the previous body text cannot be recovered from this log or anywhere else."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Very large values are shortened, and the entry is marked as truncated."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Complicated database updates are stored as the command that ran, without before and after values."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "If a plugin changes a setting or custom field the normal way and, in the same request, also alters that same row directly in the database — for example switching whether the setting loads on every page — only the value change is recorded. This applies when \"Capture raw database writes\" is on."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "If one request makes more than 200 direct database writes, recording stops there and a single summary entry is added."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "If a plugin cancels a batch of changes part-way through, a few entries may describe changes that were undone. The reverse can also happen: genuine changes made earlier in the same request, before the cancelled part even began, can be lost from the log along with the cancelled ones."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "When a BuddyPress activity item is deleted, we record that it happened but not what it said. Deleted users, comments, settings and WooCommerce products do keep a record of what they were. The one exception is a network-wide setting on a multisite network: WordPress removes it before it tells us, so that entry says the previous value was not captured rather than implying it was empty."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "When a custom field is deleted, we normally capture its value first so the entry shows what was removed. If another plugin interferes with that step, the entry honestly shows that a value was removed without being able to say what it was, rather than guessing it was empty."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "On a single site (not part of a network), a change to a network-wide setting is labelled as an ordinary setting change rather than as network-wide. The change itself is still recorded in full — only the label is affected."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Depends on your settings"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "\"Capture raw database writes\" is off until you turn it on, so changes plugins make directly to the database are not recorded by default."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Choosing to record only a small fixed list of options means plugin settings changes are not recorded anywhere."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Turning off extra field capture drops custom fields on categories, users and comments, and network-wide settings."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Routine background values are never recorded — scheduled-task bookkeeping and temporary cached data."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Hidden on purpose, to keep secrets safe"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Passwords, API keys and access tokens show as [REDACTED]. You can see that a secret changed, but not what it changed to."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Login and password tables are never read directly. User changes are recorded separately, with sensitive fields hidden."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "On a WooCommerce order, the customer's name, company, street address, postcode, email address and phone number are hidden. Town, county or state, and country are kept, so you can still see a delivery or tax area change. This log is separate from WooCommerce's own tools for handling a customer's personal-data requests."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "How long entries are kept"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Normal entries are kept for 30 days and direct-database entries for 7 days. Both are adjustable, but this is not a permanent archive."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "Only standard WordPress content can be restored from history. Entries for a plugin's own database tables are a record, not an undo."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:5
msgid "What is not recorded here"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of documented capture limits.
#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
#, js-format
msgid "%d known gap in what the change history captures. Read it before relying on the log."
msgid_plural "%d known gaps in what the change history captures. Read them before relying on the log."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Controls what the change history captures. Turning capture on or off entirely, and how long rows are kept, stay on the main Settings page."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Save capture settings"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Option recording mode"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Which wp_options (and network option) writes get a change-history row. The recommended mode records every option except known churn (transients, cron, scheduler noise); the legacy mode records only a small fixed allowlist of core settings."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Extended meta capture"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Capture term, user and comment meta changes, and network (site) options."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Post meta is always captured. Session tokens and transient-like user meta are never recorded."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Capture raw database writes"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Record custom-table and raw SQL writes made during MCP tool calls (Layer 3 interceptor)."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Opt-in. Catches plugin writes that bypass WordPress hooks (custom tables, direct SQL). Sensitive tables (users, credentials) are never captured; sensitive columns are redacted. Only writes made through MCP tool calls are ever recorded."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Recommended if you run plugins that remove WordPress hooks before writing (SureCart does this). Their hooks are re-armed automatically and a \"hooks reasserted\" entry is logged, but the re-arm happens after the call, so with this setting off those writes leave no before/after record at all — only the notice that it happened."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Raw-write retention"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
#: assets/build/page-settings.js:8
msgid "days"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Raw database rows are high-volume, so they are pruned on their own shorter schedule (default 7 days; 0 disables pruning). Semantic rows keep the main change history retention."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Record external write intent"
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "When a write-shaped tool call produces no local database change but did contact a remote service, record a marker row."
msgstr ""

#: assets/build/page-settings.js:6
msgid "Covers plugins that store their data in an external SaaS. The marker shows \"Remote change — local before/after not available\" with the contacted hosts and redacted call arguments."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of deployed settings whose value is invalid.
#: assets/build/page-settings.js:7
#, js-format
